Bilinear interpolation (inside the cell)

Derivation 1D
(y1 - y0)/ (x1 -x0) = (y - y0)/ (x - x0)
=> y = y0 + (y1 - y0) / (x1 - x0) * (x - x0)


We combine the 4 corner features:

fl​(x,y)=(1−u)(1−v)f00+u(1−v)f10+(1−u)vf01+uvf11
	​
Output:

fl(x,y)∈RF
So each level produces a small feature vector.


Bilinear interpolation:

f_l = (1-0.92)(1-0.68) · [0.3, 0.7]   ← f00, weight = 0.08 * 0.32 = 0.026
    +    0.92 (1-0.68) · [0.5, 0.2]   ← f10, weight = 0.92 * 0.32 = 0.294
    +  (1-0.92) 0.68   · [0.1, 0.9]   ← f01, weight = 0.08 * 0.68 = 0.054
    +    0.92 · 0.68   · [0.8, 0.4]   ← f11, weight = 0.92 * 0.68 = 0.626
Computing each term:


0.026 · [0.3, 0.7] = [0.008, 0.018]
0.294 · [0.5, 0.2] = [0.147, 0.059]
0.054 · [0.1, 0.9] = [0.005, 0.049]
0.626 · [0.8, 0.4] = [0.501, 0.250]

